    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263-a1">

                <pb facs="0325" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg265"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 327.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hanotaux to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ambassador</hi>: By a letter dated April 23d last
                    your excellency was kind enough to inform me of the importance attached by you
                    to the text of the sentence rendered by the court-martial at Tamatave against
                    Mr. Waller, formerly consul of the United States at Madagascar.</p>
                <p>The minister of marine has just transmitted to me the document in question and I
                    hasten to address herewith a copy to your excellency.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Hanotaux</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
